### AUTH SERVICE  ·  http://localhost:3000/auth
###
### Identity lives here. Everything else in BookVerse trusts the gateway to
### have checked a token; this is where the token comes from.
###
### Cookies (refreshToken, sessionId) are set by signup/login and resent
### automatically by the REST Client.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = amr@example.com
@password = password123


### Sign up  →  201, sets cookies, returns user + tokens
### Already registered?  →  400 "email already exists"
# @name signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Amr Nashaat",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### Log in  →  200
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

@accessToken = {{login.response.body.data.tokens.accessToken}}


### Wrong password  →  400 "something is wrong with email or password"
### Deliberately vague: it must not reveal whether the email exists.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}


### Refresh  →  200, new access token from the refreshToken cookie
### 401 if that cookie is missing — log in above first.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh


### Log out  →  204, clears the session and the cookies
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
